id=a52sxq_semantic_search_core
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Samsung Semantic Search Core
author=kusti420
description=UNTESTED-ON-DEVICE (Galaxy AI port 2026-10-16). Samsung Semantic Search Core (com.samsung.android.ssco, provider content://com.samsung.android.ssco.models) is the text-embedding engine behind Settings natural-language search / "in-app assist" (SecSettingsIntelligence SSESearchManager), Smart Suggestions search (Finder) and My Files semantic search; services.jar, SmartCapture and SamsungAiCore query it too. The S26 Ultra ships it only as a CSC "restore" app (prism restore_<CSC>.json) that Galaxy Store installs during setup, so the port never gets it, and the Store stub API refuses it ("not approved as stub"). Upstream UN1CA's paradigm mod ships the Galaxy S25+ build as a system priv-app; this does the same with that build (prebuilts/samsung/pa2qxxx, 4.0.00.7): a CPU TFLite sentence encoder (v0.37_100k_vocab_256_token.tflite + SentencePiece, libtensorflowlite_jni), no NPU runtime, no privileged platform permissions. Caveat: the S26U callers also know newer provider methods (GET_EMBEDDING_CONFIG, GET_STORED_EMBEDDING_VERSION, services.jar GET_RAW_EMBEDDING) and the FUNCTION_INFO meta-data that 4.0 lacks; Smart Suggestions catches call failures, so the expected worst case is "no semantic results", not a crash. Galaxy Store can update it in place.
